{
  "info": {
    "name": "automotive-workshop-api",
    "description": "Manual test collection for automotive-workshop-api, generated from the routes registered in cmd/api/main.go and each feature's RegisterRoutes.\n\nGetting started:\n1. Bring the stack up (docker compose up -d) and load docs/seed.sql.\n2. Run Auth > Login: the test script stores access_token in {{token}}, used by every protected request.\n3. Run the create requests in order (Customer > Vehicle > Service > Product > Service order); each stores the returned id in a collection variable consumed by the following ones.\n\nAuthentication:\n- Bearer JWT for every route, including Customers and POST /api/v1/service-orders (wrapped in requireAuth on 2026-08-26, CLAUDE.md section 1).\n- The /acompanhamento routes deliberately use the X-Tracking-Token header instead of the JWT.\n\nThe sample payloads use fictitious data. Do not store real customer data, real documents, or production credentials in this file.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health check",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Public liveness probe. Returns {\"status\":\"ok\"}.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Public. Credentials come from docs/seed.sql (dev only). The test script stores access_token in the {{token}} variable used by every protected request.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"admin@workshop.local\",\n  \"password\": \"admin123\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (body.access_token) { pm.collectionVariables.set(\"token\", body.access_token); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Me",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/me",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "me"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Protected. Returns the authenticated administrative user."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
